---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const title = "Privacy & Data Protection";
const description = "How Vision Hub demos handle data, consent, and integrity in compliance with EU and Swedish law.";

const CONTACT_NAME  = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_NAME  || 'Your Name';
const CONTACT_EMAIL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL || 'your.email@example.com';
---

<SiteLayout {title} {description}>
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:800px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 16px;">
    <h1>Privacy & Data Protection</h1>

    <p>
      This page describes how <b>Vision Hub</b> processes data in compliance with the
      <b>European Union’s General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679)</b>
      and Sweden’s national implementation, <b>Dataskyddsförordningen</b>.
      The system follows the integrity principles promoted by
      <b>Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten (IMY)</b>, Sweden’s data protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Purpose of the demonstrations</h2>
    <p>
      The Vision Hub installation at Luleå University of Technology showcases interactive
      <b>AI-based research demonstrations</b> that operate in real time. The purpose is purely
      educational and research-oriented — to illustrate how modern AI systems can detect
      objects, track movement, recognize handwritten text, or estimate values using machine learning.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Type of data processed</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on the demonstration, Vision Hub processes either:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Live camera frames</b> from a fixed on-site camera (for computer vision demos), or
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>User-provided non-identifying input data</b> (for non-visual demos such as house price estimation).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      For camera-based demonstrations, video frames are analyzed instantly in memory to produce
      visual overlays (such as boxes or skeletons) or on-screen text output (for handwritten text recognition).
      <u>No videos or images are saved or exported.</u>
    </p>

    <p>
      For non-visual demonstrations (e.g. house price estimation), only anonymous numerical inputs
      (such as housing features) are processed by a machine learning model. These inputs are not intended
      to identify any person and are not linked to an account or identity.
    </p>

    <h3>Demo-specific processing</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Object detection & pose estimation:</b> live camera frames analyzed in real time to display
        bounding boxes or skeletal keypoints.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Arabic handwritten text recognition:</b> live camera frames analyzed to recognize handwritten
        characters; no recognized text or images are stored.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>House price estimation:</b> anonymous, user-provided numerical inputs (e.g. area, room count,
        location indicators) processed by a machine learning model; no camera, no personal identifiers.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Legal basis for processing</h2>
    <p>
      For camera-based demonstrations, processing is based on <b>Article 6(1)(a) of the GDPR</b> — your
      <b>explicit consent</b> to participate in a live demonstration.
      The processing serves no commercial or surveillance purpose.
    </p>

    <p>
      Participation is entirely voluntary. You may withdraw consent at any time by asking a staff member
      to stop the demo or by stepping away from the camera area.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Consent management</h2>
    <p>
      When a visitor gives consent to participate in a camera-based demo, a short-lived <b>consent token</b>
      is created within the <b>local demo environment</b> (on the lab’s computer). This token:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Is valid for approximately 10 minutes.</li>
      <li>Contains no personal or identifying data.</li>
      <li>Is used only to temporarily authorize the live demo on this device.</li>
      <li>Expires automatically and is not retained after the session.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      No consent tokens are shared externally. Consent is <b>local to the installation</b> and cannot be
      linked to any external system, individual, or network.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data retention and storage</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No image, audio, or video data is stored or transmitted.</li>
      <li>No persistent tracking identifiers (e.g. cookies for analytics) are used.</li>
      <li>
        Short-lived consent tokens may be stored locally on the device solely to manage demo access and
        expire automatically.
      </li>
      <li>The system does not perform identity verification, face recognition, or biometric identification.</li>
      <li>All AI processing occurs in real time and primarily in memory.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The demo computer is used solely for on-site research and exhibition purposes. Network access is
      restricted to what is needed to operate the demo environment.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights under EU and Swedish law</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR and Swedish data protection rules, you have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Be informed about how data is used in the demonstration.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time (for camera-based demos).</li>
      <li>
        Request erasure or restriction of any personal data (generally not applicable here, as no personal
        data is stored).
      </li>
      <li>Contact <b>Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten (IMY)</b> if you believe your rights are violated.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Since camera frames are not stored or transferred, withdrawing consent simply ends the live session.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Contact information</h2>
    <p>
      For any question about data protection and privacy in Vision Hub, please contact:
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>{CONTACT_NAME}</b><br/>
      Vision Hub Project – Luleå University of Technology<br/>
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:32px;color:#9cb0d8;font-size:0.9rem;">
      Last updated: December 2025 — aligned with the EU GDPR and Swedish data protection rules (Dataskyddsförordningen).
    </p>
  </div>

  <link rel="modulepreload" href="/scripts/consent-widget.js" />
  <script type="module" src="/scripts/consent-widget.js"></script>

  <h1>Privacy & Consent</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    This station uses short-lived local consent tokens for camera-based demos. You can review and withdraw them below.
  </p>

  <!-- Configure via attributes -->
  <consent-status
    demos="yolo,pose,price,chang"
    orch=":8090"
    token="dev-token"
    stop="true"
    intro="Below is your consent status on this station. Tokens are short-lived and stored locally. You can withdraw at any time."
  ></consent-status>
</SiteLayout>
